{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>לא יחבל רחים.</b> Deficient one word, and it is as though it were written לא יחבול החובל (the creditor shall not take in pledge). Another interpretation: it concludes from the preceding — after he was given permission to remain in his house, he must be careful <b>לא יחבל רחים ורכב</b> of those who go forth to the army, for he is taking in pledge their very life, for what will they do in war without them?" "<b>רחים ורכב.</b> Not these two alone, but any object that is the tool of one's craft." "<b>[לא יחבל רחים ורכב</b> — that it is forbidden to take in pledge his wife]. רחים is written only in the plural form, like שמים, מים חיים, פנים, מלקחים, מעים. <b>[כי נפש הוא חבל</b> — the life of the soul]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase אדסליק מיניה קאי ('it concludes from it, it stands') signals that this verse's law follows from the preceding context; rendered here as 'it concludes from the preceding.'", 2 "The bracketed lemma heads and interpolations appear in the source and are preserved as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:07.182146509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}